<h2>Classification Rules</h2>
<p>
  Before building the production solution, all 29 concept and legacy <code>.cs</code> files were audited and moved to <code>archive/concept/</code> and <code>archive/legacy-cli/</code> (neither directory is compiled). Every file was classified so behavior could be ported into <code>src/</code> deliberately:
</p>

{{ specTable({
  caption: "SOURCE INVENTORY CLASSIFICATION TAXONOMY",
  headers: ["Classification", "Definition", "Integration Action"],
  rows: [
    ["<strong>Authoritative</strong>", "The latest revision of a concern; its behavior is the specification for that domain.", "Ported into the target project under the listed tracker task and adapted to <code>System.CommandLine</code> and ADR 0002."],
    ["<strong>Merge input</strong>", "An older or parallel revision that retains behavior missing from the latest revision.", "Unique behavior is folded into the authoritative port; duplicate scaffolding is discarded."],
    ["<strong>Superseded patch</strong>", "Fully replaced by a later revision with no unique behavior remaining.", "Not ported; retained only in <code>archive/</code> for historical traceability."],
    ["<strong>Design-only archive</strong>", "A design document or concept module with no scheduled task or with a design rejected by ADRs.", "Reference material only; ported only when a dedicated tracker task is scheduled."]
  ]
}) }}

